  "id": "469059303",
  "subject": [
    "Roman road"
  ],
  "title": "Via Herculia",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 44 H3 Via Herculia",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/road"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The\u00a0Via Herculia is included on maps 44 (44 H3) and 45 (45 B2) in the\u00a0<em>Barrington Atlas</em>. N. Purcell makes no explicit comment on the road in the directory entry for map 44, referring readers to map 45. The map 45 compilers also do not expressly address the road in their commentary, but it features prominently in the area covered by map 45. Buck (1971) summarizes the evidence for the road and posits that it was a\u00a0<em>via publica </em>at\u00a0the time of Diocletian and Maximian Herculius.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A Roman road known through epigraphic attestations, the Via Herculia connected Aquilonia and Aequum Tuticum.",
  "reprPoint": [
